WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.498
This episode focuses on housing measures.

2
00:00:03.498 --> 00:00:10.202
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:10.202 --> 00:00:13.284
Housing questions need both a unit and a universe.

4
00:00:13.284 --> 00:00:21.789
Total units, occupied units, owner-occupied units, renter-occupied units, households, and people in households support different measures.

5
00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:29.751
ACS topics include tenure, vacancy, structure type, year built, costs, value, rent, rooms, bedrooms, vehicles, and housing-cost burden.

6
00:00:29.751 --> 00:00:34.411
Definitions and denominators determine whether two percentages can be compared.

7
00:00:34.411 --> 00:00:36.487
Survey evidence describes conditions.

8
00:00:36.487 --> 00:00:43.557
It does not by itself establish zoning capacity, project feasibility, legal compliance, or the City's adopted housing program.

9
00:00:43.557 --> 00:00:47.934
Pair it with local planning records while keeping each source's role distinct.

10
00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.444
Torrance application segment.

11
00:00:49.444 --> 00:00:53.141
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

12
00:00:53.141 --> 00:01:06.314
The cited City of Torrance primary source is General Plan: Housing Element materials, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/Departments-Offices/Departments-Offices/Community-Development/Planning-Division/Comprehensive-Planning/General-Plan.

13
00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:14.437
For a local analysis, use ACS housing characteristics as context, then cite the City's adopted Housing Element separately for policies, programs, and sites.

14
00:01:14.437 --> 00:01:21.779
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

15
00:01:21.779 --> 00:01:31.711
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

16
00:01:31.711 --> 00:01:34.940
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

17
00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:39.693
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

18
00:01:39.693 --> 00:01:43.958
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

19
00:01:43.958 --> 00:01:49.929
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

20
00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:54.255
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
